---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import photo from '../assets/burhan-kapasi.jpg';
import { AUTHOR, SITE } from '../site.config';

const schema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'Person',
	name: AUTHOR.name,
	jobTitle: AUTHOR.role,
	url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
	image: `${SITE.url}${AUTHOR.photo}`,
	sameAs: [AUTHOR.linkedin, AUTHOR.website],
};
---

<PageLayout
	title="About Rankfolk"
	eyebrow="About"
	description="Rankfolk helps small business owners and contractors get more customers online, with plain English guides based on real client work."
>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

	<h2>Why Rankfolk exists</h2>
	<p>
		Most marketing advice is written for big companies with big budgets. Small business owners get buried in jargon, tool
		pitches and "growth hacks" that don't apply to a roofing company, a dental clinic or a local cleaner.
	</p>
	<p>
		Rankfolk is different. Every guide answers one practical question an owner actually has, like how to show up on Google
		Maps, what a website needs to turn visitors into calls, or which tools are worth paying for. The goal is simple: {SITE.tagline.toLowerCase()}.
	</p>

	<h2>Who writes it</h2>
	<figure class="not-prose float-none mx-auto my-8 w-full max-w-xs sm:float-right sm:my-2 sm:ml-8 sm:w-64">
		<Image src={photo} alt={`${AUTHOR.name}, founder of Mago Labs`} width={520} height={650} class="pop-lg aspect-[4/5] w-full rotate-2 rounded-[1.75rem] object-cover" />
		<figcaption class="mt-4 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-muted">{AUTHOR.name}, {AUTHOR.role}</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<p>
		Rankfolk is written by <strong>{AUTHOR.name}</strong>, founder of <a href={AUTHOR.website} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mago Labs</a>.
	</p>
	<p>{AUTHOR.bio}</p>
	<p>
		Before building websites full time, Burhan spent over eight years in sales and partnerships at banks, fintech
		companies and an insurer. That background shapes how Rankfolk is written: focused on results, honest about costs, and
		clear about what is worth your time.
	</p>

	<h2>How we write our guides</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Based on real work.</strong> Advice comes from building and ranking real small business websites.</li>
		<li><strong>Checked against official sources.</strong> Google's own documentation comes first for anything about Search or Maps.</li>
		<li><strong>Kept up to date.</strong> Guides are reviewed and updated when platforms change.</li>
		<li><strong>Honest about money.</strong> Some links are affiliate links. They never decide what we recommend. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		Questions, corrections or topic ideas are always welcome. <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> or connect with
		Burhan on <a href={AUTHOR.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener me">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
</PageLayout>
